OL,3,GNEWSAWoman who feared losing leg raises
OL,4,Acare concerns
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman whose leg was saved from
OL,7,Famputation by community nurses has
OL,8,Fraised concerns after experiencing
OL,9,Fdelays and missed appointments in the
OL,10,Fcare she relies on.
OL,12,FDeborah Williams, 73, from Swindon,
OL,13,Fsaid early detection previously
OL,14,Fprevented her leg ulcers from
OL,15,Fdeteriorating but appointments had
OL,16,Fbecome harder to obtain recently.
OL,18,FHer experience is among more than 100
OL,19,Fcomplaints from patients and staff to
OL,20,FWiltshire MP Brian Mathew, reporting
OL,21,Fdelays to urgent nursing care and
OL,22,Fgrowing referral backlogs.
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
